{
  "@context": {
    "schema": "https://schema.org/"
  },
  "@type": "Note",
  "@id": "note:notion-365",
  "title": "Unit Testing Prompt",
  "status": "draft",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Unit Testing Prompt"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "You are tasked with fixing failing unit tests. Your goal is to make the tests pass through proper implementation, not by taking shortcuts or over-fitting to the specific test cases."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Key Requirements:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**No Over-fitting:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-9",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Don't hardcode specific values or responses that only work for the current test cases"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-6",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Implement the actual business logic and algorithms as intended"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-7",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Consider edge cases and scenarios beyond what's explicitly tested"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-8",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Write code that would work correctly for similar inputs not covered by tests"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**No Shortcuts:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-15",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-11",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Don't modify or comment out test assertions to make them \"pass\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-12",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Don't mock or stub functionality that should be genuinely implemented"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-13",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Don't use try/catch blocks to silently ignore errors unless error handling is the intended behavior"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-14",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Don't return hardcoded values without proper computation"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Proper Implementation Approach:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. Analyze what each failing test is actually trying to verify"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-18",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. Understand the expected behavior and business requirements"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. Implement the underlying functionality correctly"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-20",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. Ensure your solution handles the general case, not just the test scenarios"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-21",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "5. Consider performance, maintainability, and code quality"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-22",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Before submitting your solution:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-27",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-23",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Run all tests to ensure you haven't broken existing functionality"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-24",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Verify your implementation makes logical sense beyond just passing tests"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-25",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Check that your code follows established patterns and conventions in the codebase"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-26",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Consider if your solution would handle reasonable variations of the input"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-28",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Remember: The tests are specifications for the desired behavior. Your job is to implement that behavior correctly, not to game the tests."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}